A joint template and a direct producer of one of its outputs are not ambiguous:
the direct producer supplies that concrete type, so the template is instantiated
only for its still-needed output, lifting the parameter the direct-supplied
result would otherwise have pinned. AlsoKeyInt supplies Key[int], so NewKVPair is
taken at a lifted T (to produce Value[string]) rather than pinned to int, leaving
Key[int] to the single direct producer instead of producing it twice.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
-- example.com/app/a.go --
package app

type Key[T any] struct{}
type Value[U any] struct{}
type Sink struct{}

//plumb:build
func NewKVPair[T, U any]() (Key[T], Value[U]) { return Key[T]{}, Value[U]{} }

//plumb:build
func AlsoKeyInt() Key[int] { return Key[int]{} }

//plumb:build
func NewSink(k Key[int], v Value[string]) *Sink { return nil }
